 good works and misery avoided.","anchor":"وإنما أورد من أوصافهم عدم إيمانهم بالآخرة واقتصر عليه لأن دين الحق مبني على أساس أن للإنسان حياة خالدة","mentions":[]},{"verses":["23:74"],"words":["عن الصراط"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Religious duties require accounting and recompense on Judgment Day; those who deny it see religion as futile and life as material pleasure, so desire governs them regardless of truth.","anchor":"والتكليف لا يتم إلا بحساب وجزاء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["23:74"],"words":["لناكبون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Their lack of faith in the afterlife leaves them pursuing whim whether it agrees with truth or opposes it.","anchor":"ولازم ذلك أن يكون المتبع عندهم الهوى وافق الحق أو خالفه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["23:75","23:76"],"words":["ولو رحمناهم"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"الراغب","stance":"reports","claim":"Al-Rāghib defines lijāj as persistence and obstinacy in a forbidden act, and ʿamah as bewildered hesitation in a matter.","anchor":"والعمه التردد في الأمر من التحير، ذكرهما الراغب","mentions":[]},{"verses":["23:76"],"words":["فما استكانوا لربهم"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"مجمع البيان","stance":"reports","claim":"Majmaʿ al-Bayān glosses istikāna as submission, an istifʿāl form from kawn: they did not seek to be in a submissive state.","anchor":"وفي المجمع الاستكانة الخضوع وهو استفعال من الكون","mentions":[]},{"verses":["23:75","23:76"],"words":["ولو رحمناهم وكشفنا ما بهم من ضر"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Even if God relieved their distress, they would answer with no gratitude, persist in rebellion and perplexity, and gain no benefit from mercy, just as threats do not benefit them.","anchor":"لو رحمناهم وكشفنا ما بهم من ضر لم يرجعوا بمقابلة ذلك الشكر بل أصروا على تمردهم عن الحق","mentions":[]},{"verses":["23:76"],"words":["فما استكانوا لربهم وما يتضرعون"],"type":"interpretation","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The punishment was a light chastisement that did not cut them off from ordinary means, as indicated by the following verse; this avoids the objection that desperate people instinctively return to God.","anchor":"والمراد بالعذاب العذاب الخفيف الذي لا ينقطع به الإنسان عن عامة الأسباب بقرينة ما في الآية التالية","mentions":["23:77"]},{"verses":["23:76"],"words":["فما استكانوا لربهم وما يتضرعون"],"type":"links","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The apparent problem is that people instinctively turn to God in distress when cut off from ordinary causes, a pattern repeated elsewhere in the Qur’an.","anchor":"لا يرد أن الرجوع إلى الله تعالى عند الاضطرار والانقطاع عن الأسباب","mentions":[]}]}
